    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nConstructed in 2016, Makasi is a truly exceptional detached residence of striking contemporary design, set amidst approximately 0.147 hectares of mature private gardens in a highly sought-after residential setting just off the Swords Road. Ideally positioned within walking distance of Malahide Village and its excellent range of amenities, this remarkable home offers a rare combination of architectural flair, privacy, and modern family living.\n\nExpertly designed by ODKM Architects and built to an exceptional standard by Clanforce Construction , Makasi is a home of immense style and individuality. Contemporary in concept, the property is defined by light-filled interiors, clean architectural lines, and expansive picture windows that frame the beautifully landscaped gardens. Every aspect of the home has been thoughtfully curated, with no expense spared in its presentation and finish, resulting in a residence of outstanding quality and warmth.\n\nDesigned over a combination of single and two-storey living spaces and extending to approximately 222 sq. m., the accommodation is both elegant and highly functional. A bright and welcoming reception hall immediately impresses with its high ceilings and stunning gallery-style landing with integrated library space overhead.\n\nThe reception hall flows effortlessly into a magnificent bespoke kitchen designed by Dean Cooper, complete with premium appliances and beautifully crafted cabinetry. Large picture windows overlook the extensive Blue Molasse sandstone patio, seamlessly connecting the interior with the surrounding gardens. Open in design, this impressive space steps down into a superb living area featuring dramatic corner windows and multiple patio doors opening to the rear garden, creating the perfect environment for modern family living and entertaining.\n\nA well-appointed utility room is positioned just off the kitchen with direct access to the rear garden. Also located off the reception hall is a spacious playroom/TV room, along with a versatile lounge or fourth bedroom featuring patio doors to the garden.\n\nA striking precast reinforced concrete staircase leads to the upper level, where a beautifully designed gallery landing serves as a sophisticated library and home office space. There are three generously proportioned bedrooms on this floor, including a stunning principal suite complete with a large dressing room and luxurious ensuite bathroom. A spacious family bathroom completes the accommodation.\n\nApproached through electronic security gates, the grounds are a standout feature of this remarkable home. Sweeping lawns, mature trees, and established hedging provide exceptional privacy and tranquillity, while a gravel driveway offers extensive secure parking and includes an EV charging point.\n\nTo the rear, an extensive split-level patio paved in Blue Molasse sandstone has been designed to maximise the sunny south-facing orientation, creating a superb outdoor entertaining space. The gardens are further enhanced by a purpose-built garden shed (22 sq. m) and a separate bin store.\n\nAdding further appeal, planning permission has been granted onsite for the construction of a separate single-storey detached two-bedroom dwelling extending to approximately 138 sq. m., complete with a new vehicular entrance onto the Swords Road and off-street parking (F26A/0052E). This presents a rare and exciting opportunity for additional family accommodation, guest residence, or future development potential.\n\nCombining cutting-edge design, exceptional craftsmanship, and a prime location close to Malahide Village, Makasi is a truly outstanding contemporary residence. Viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the quality, setting, and lifestyle this unique home has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nReception Hall - 4.75m x 2.39m\nHeight- 5.35mWelcoming reception hall, light filled with feature overhead gallery/library. Superb tiled floor, picture windows overlooking rear garden, staircase to upper floor. Sliding glass door to kitchen/lounge\n\nGuest WC - 2.11m x 1.38m\nWC, WHB, Vanity Mirror, Storage Press, Tiled floor\n\nInner hall - 3.92m x 1.00m\nPicture windows overlooking rear garden and patio area\n\nLounge/Bedroom 4 - 4.51m x 4.31m\nDual purpose room with large picture window and sliding patio door to rear garden\n\nTV Room/Playroom - 3.82m x 3.19m\nGlass pivot door to rear garden and patio, glass wall to reception hall\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 6.27m x 5.01m\nStunning open plan kitchen, bespoke in design by Dean Cooper Kitchens with excellent fitted press units including solid dovetailed larder drawers with black stain and natural lacquer finish, Silestone work surface and upstand (12mm Doraus with a suede finish) including the island mitred gables, top quality appliances including Quooker tap, Caple Downdraft Extractor with 4 ring hob, Liebherr integrated larder and separate fridge freezer, Miele steam oven, Miele oven, Miele heated drawer, Siemens integrated dishwasher, picture windows overlooking the mature gardens and patio, fully tiled floor and steps to family area, patio door to rear garden\n\nFamily Area - 5.02m x 4.30m\nA most relaxing family area with tiled floor and dual aspect windows including a feature corner window and patio door to the south facing garden\n\nUtility Room - 3.16m x 2.56m\nHidden door from kitchen, with press units, tiled floor, door to rear garden\n\nLanding - 4.47m x 2.10m\nGallery style landing with glass feature\n\nLibrary/Reading Area - 2.88m x 2.68m\nBright light filled library/reading area with picture window to front\n\nInner landing hall - 9.86m x 1.12m\nLeads to bedrooms\n\nPrincipal Bedroom - 5.25m x 4.16m\nSuperb principal bedroom with dual aspect windows and sliding door to South and West overlooking the extensive patio and gardens, floor to ceiling built in wardrobes, recessed spotlights on ceiling, electronic blinds (including blackout blinds)\n\nEnsuite - 2.53m x 1.63m\nStunning ensuite with Villeroy and Boch sanitary ware, tiled floor with underfloor heating, wet shower, WC, WHB\n\nDressing Area - 1.88m x 1.64m\nSpacious dressing area\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.50m x 2.94m\nFreestanding wardrobes, large picture window overlooking gardens\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.34m x 3.51m\nBuilt in wardrobes, window overlooking gardens\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.97m x 2.57m\nExcellent family bathroom with Villeroy & Boch sanitary ware, under floor heating, His & Hers WHB, large rain shower, WC\n\n"
      },
